<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farhud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Farhud was a violent pogrom against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> on 1–2 June 1941, in the power vacuum after the fall of Rashid Ali's pro-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> government and before British troops entered the city. At least 180 Jews were killed, many more were injured and their property was looted. It marked a turning point for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>'s ancient Jewish community, most of whom left for Israel in 1950–1951.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farhud.jpg" alt="Farhud" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farhud_mass_grave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
